WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:00.876
(upbeat music)

00:00:00.876 --> 00:00:03.935
- [Voiceover] This is
Lilly, an African penguin.

00:00:03.935 --> 00:00:06.030
She's a jackass.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.528
No, really.

00:00:07.528 --> 00:00:11.695
African penguins are commonly
known as jackass penguins.

00:00:14.532 --> 00:00:19.246
Their nickname comes from the
donkey-like sounds they make.

00:00:19.246 --> 00:00:20.911
But they're no donkey.

00:00:20.911 --> 00:00:24.631
These little guys grow up to
only a little over two feet

00:00:24.631 --> 00:00:27.380
and weigh up to eight pounds.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.400
They're only found on the
southwestern coast of Africa,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.645
where they're a popular
sight for tourists.

00:00:34.645 --> 00:00:37.794
However, experts say that
if their population decline

00:00:37.794 --> 00:00:42.209
isn't stopped, they'll
be extinct in 15 years

00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:45.709
You see, African penguins
are pursuit divers

00:00:45.709 --> 00:00:48.542
and feed mostly on fish and squid.

00:00:49.446 --> 00:00:52.544
But because of competition
from commercial fishing,

00:00:52.544 --> 00:00:57.245
they have to go further and
further to find enough to eat.

00:00:57.245 --> 00:01:00.602
That, combined with
encroaching human development,

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.237
poaching for eggs and oil spills,

00:01:03.237 --> 00:01:07.158
are all taking a toll on its population.

00:01:07.158 --> 00:01:08.716
This is the African penguin.

00:01:08.716 --> 00:01:11.383
(upbeat music)

